r, Exquisite, Quest, Require.","source":"Webster’s Unabridged Dictionary (1913)","sourceUrl":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/29765"},"quest":{"syllables":["quest"],"etymology":"OF. queste, F. quête, fr. L. quaerere, quaesitum, to seek for, to ask. Cf. Query, Question.","source":"Webster’s Unabridged Dictionary (1913)","sourceUrl":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/29765"},"quester":{"syllables":["quest","er"],"etymology":"","source":"Webster’s Unabridged Dictionary (1913)","sourceUrl":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/29765"},"question":{"syllables":["ques","tion"],"etymology":"F., fr. L. quaestio, fr. quaerere, quaesitum, to seek for, ask, inquire. See Quest, n.","source":"Webster’s Unabridged Dictionary (1913)","sourceUrl":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/29765"},"questionable":{"syllables":["ques","tion","a","ble"],"etymology":"","source":"Webster’s Unabridged Dictionary (1913)","sourceUrl":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/29765"},"questionably":{"syllables":["ques","tion","a","bly"],"etymology":"","source":"Webster’s Unabridged Dictionary (1913)","sourceUrl":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/29765"},"questioner":{"syllables":["ques","tion","er"],"etymology":"","source":"Webster’s Unabridged Dictionary (1913)","sourceUrl":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/29765"},"questionnaire":{"syllables":["ques","tion","naire"],"etymology":"Borrowed from French questionnaire , from Late Latin quaestionarius , from quaestio (English question ) + -arius , from quaerō ( “ to question ” ) (English query ).","source":"Webster’s Unabridged Dictionary (1913)","sourceUrl":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/29765","etymologySource":"English Wiktionary","etymologySourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?title=questionnaire&oldid=93132132"},"queue":{"syllables":["queue"],"etymology":"F. See Cue.","source":"Webster’s Unabridged Dictionary (1913)","sourceUrl":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/29765"},"quibble":{"syllables":["quib","ble"],"etymology":"Probably fr. quib, quip, bu